1
00:00:38,539 --> 00:00:41,959
MY BIAS, MY BOSS

2
00:00:47,172 --> 00:00:51,259
Do you have to apologize
because you said something mean?

3
00:00:51,260 --> 00:00:52,510
The sooner, the better.

4
00:00:52,511 --> 00:00:54,137
Apologies expire too.

5
00:00:54,721 --> 00:00:56,640
They'll mean nothing
if you wait too long.

6
00:01:13,240 --> 00:01:14,324
Where did she go?

7
00:01:16,159 --> 00:01:17,160
Where is she?

8
00:01:22,749 --> 00:01:23,875
Is she on the rooftop?

9
00:01:31,216 --> 00:01:32,884
No, it's not messy. I was gentle.

10
00:02:02,873 --> 00:02:05,083
I'll think of a wish, Da-reum.

11
00:02:08,253 --> 00:02:09,254
"Da-reum"?

12
00:02:22,351 --> 00:02:23,352
What brings you here this late?

13
00:02:23,518 --> 00:02:24,728
I came because I missed you.

14
00:02:28,607 --> 00:02:31,067
Ms. Nam, why are you up here?

15
00:02:31,068 --> 00:02:32,069
What?

16
00:02:34,655 --> 00:02:35,656
Oh, I...

17
00:02:37,199 --> 00:02:38,949
I came to get this banner

18
00:02:38,950 --> 00:02:41,703
then ran into Director Lee
by coincidence.

19
00:02:43,705 --> 00:02:44,706
Please excuse me.

20
00:02:51,880 --> 00:02:53,548
Goodbye, then.

21
00:02:57,219 --> 00:02:58,220
Bye, Da-reum.

22
00:03:02,724 --> 00:03:05,685
Aren't you being a bit too friendly?
After all, she's an employee.

23
00:03:05,686 --> 00:03:06,852
I wasn't, really.

24
00:03:06,853 --> 00:03:08,772
You patted her head
and spoke in a casual tone.

25
00:03:09,272 --> 00:03:10,564
Do you think she's your fan?

26
00:03:10,565 --> 00:03:13,526
She had something in her hair,
so I just pulled it out.

27
00:03:13,527 --> 00:03:16,905
We're at work.
I'm worried people will talk.

28
00:03:18,949 --> 00:03:20,075
Are you jealous?

29
00:03:20,784 --> 00:03:21,909
Jealous, my foot.

30
00:03:21,910 --> 00:03:23,202
All right. I'll be more careful.

31
00:03:23,203 --> 00:03:24,453
- Sorry.
- Watch out.

32
00:03:24,454 --> 00:03:25,497
Okay.

33
00:03:31,670 --> 00:03:33,588
EPISODE 4

34
00:03:35,590 --> 00:03:37,300
Oh, my. Ms. Da-reum.

35
00:03:37,676 --> 00:03:38,719
Why are you taking that?

36
00:03:45,642 --> 00:03:48,227
Wait, Ms. Da-reum.
You must be on Team Chan.

37
00:03:48,228 --> 00:03:49,646
- Right?
- Sorry?

38
00:03:51,022 --> 00:03:52,606
No, not really.

39
00:03:52,607 --> 00:03:56,695
My friend needed this
for banner recycling.

40
00:03:57,237 --> 00:03:58,238
I am

41
00:03:59,364 --> 00:04:00,782
on Team Ha-gi.

42
00:04:03,952 --> 00:04:05,328
- Really?
- Yes.

43
00:04:08,582 --> 00:04:11,250
Why is the management
more popular than the celebrity

44
00:04:11,251 --> 00:04:12,794
in this company?

45
00:04:13,545 --> 00:04:14,588
Right?

46
00:04:14,963 --> 00:04:16,381
- Goodbye, then.
- Goodbye.

47
00:04:16,715 --> 00:04:18,133
Have a great night.

48
00:04:28,435 --> 00:04:29,561
So heavy.

49
00:04:31,188 --> 00:04:33,190
Don't be so weak, Nam Da-reum.

50
00:04:33,690 --> 00:04:35,817
You're carrying your Chan.

51
00:04:36,985 --> 00:04:39,863
I got this. It's not heavy at all.

52
00:04:56,922 --> 00:04:58,006
Ms. Nam.

53
00:05:01,343 --> 00:05:02,469
What are you doing?

54
00:05:05,055 --> 00:05:08,350
My friend asked me to bring this.

55
00:05:08,767 --> 00:05:10,519
So are you carrying that home?

56
00:05:11,228 --> 00:05:12,229
Yes, sir.

57
00:05:13,188 --> 00:05:15,272
I'm strong. I'll be fine.

58
00:05:15,273 --> 00:05:17,234
All right, then.

59
00:05:22,280 --> 00:05:23,990
Did he actually leave
because I said I was fine?

60
00:05:34,292 --> 00:05:35,293
Hop in.

61
00:05:35,877 --> 00:05:36,878
I'll give you a ride.

62
00:05:39,172 --> 00:05:40,298
Thank you.

63
00:05:45,804 --> 00:05:48,765
It feels like
there are three of us in the car.

64
00:05:51,268 --> 00:05:53,270
Maybe I shouldn't have hopped in.

65
00:05:53,770 --> 00:05:54,938
It's so awkward.

66
00:05:57,649 --> 00:06:00,402
There's something I must say to you.

67
00:06:01,611 --> 00:06:03,905
Sure. Please fire away.

68
00:06:07,075 --> 00:06:08,076
Actually

69
00:06:09,077 --> 00:06:10,871
I have misunderstood you for a while.

70
00:06:14,291 --> 00:06:16,167
What kind of misunderstanding?

71
00:06:19,379 --> 00:06:22,799
SE Corporation plans to launch
a fashion platform like ours soon

72
00:06:23,133 --> 00:06:24,885
and they've been taking our brands.

73
00:06:26,469 --> 00:06:29,639
- Are you serious?
- Appello's data had been leaked

74
00:06:30,891 --> 00:06:32,100
so I got a bit sensitive.

75
00:06:33,351 --> 00:06:35,603
I thought you were hiding
the fact that you worked there

76
00:06:35,604 --> 00:06:36,813
to infiltrate my business.

77
00:06:40,734 --> 00:06:41,776
Wait a second.

78
00:06:42,277 --> 00:06:43,820
Did you think

79
00:06:44,571 --> 00:06:47,908
I was some kind of spy or something?

80
00:06:51,077 --> 00:06:52,162
I'm sorry.

81
00:06:54,956 --> 00:06:56,958
I'm sorry for saying
all those harsh words to you.

82
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:00,378
- I sincerely...
- Sorry.

83
00:07:05,008 --> 00:07:06,343
He got me.

84
00:07:07,594 --> 00:07:08,803
How did you figure out...

85
00:07:10,805 --> 00:07:11,890
I was a spy?

86
00:07:13,808 --> 00:07:14,851
What?

87
00:07:20,815 --> 00:07:22,609
I'm just joking.

88
00:07:26,780 --> 00:07:29,114
I can't believe you had
such a misunderstanding.

89
00:07:29,115 --> 00:07:32,535
It's not like I'm Black Widow.

90
00:07:33,203 --> 00:07:35,455
That's why I'm apologizing.

91
00:07:35,664 --> 00:07:36,790
Please stop laughing.

92
00:07:37,165 --> 00:07:40,293
Well, I want to stop too.

93
00:07:40,919 --> 00:07:42,671
But it's too funny.

94
00:07:44,464 --> 00:07:47,007
Don't worry about it, Mr. Kang.

95
00:07:47,008 --> 00:07:49,970
I love Appello way
more than I liked them.

96
00:07:50,637 --> 00:07:53,598
I believe
our company will grow much bigger

97
00:07:54,057 --> 00:07:55,350
and far surpass SE Corporation.

98
00:07:58,228 --> 00:08:00,897
- Do you mean it?
- Of course, I do.

99
00:08:03,024 --> 00:08:06,486
Wait, should I help you find the spy?

100
00:08:08,071 --> 00:08:09,655
- You?
- Yes.

101
00:08:09,656 --> 00:08:12,993
Who knows?
I might catch a trace of that punk.

102
00:08:14,411 --> 00:08:15,453
Sure, I guess.

103
00:08:15,745 --> 00:08:17,247
Let me know if you see

104
00:08:18,373 --> 00:08:19,540
anything suspicious.

105
00:08:19,541 --> 00:08:21,418
Yes, sir. I'll do my best.

106
00:08:22,669 --> 00:08:25,088
Who is it?
Who could be doing such a thing?

107
00:08:25,505 --> 00:08:28,841
Gosh, I've only seen
people do this on TV.

108
00:08:28,842 --> 00:08:30,093
I'm so excited.

109
00:08:38,893 --> 00:08:40,311
PROJECT OUTSTANDING EMPLOYEE

110
00:08:43,690 --> 00:08:47,902
"Help out
with the logistical task for Go.co."

111
00:08:50,989 --> 00:08:52,449
"Find the spy..."

112
00:08:55,618 --> 00:08:57,327
FIND THE SPY

113
00:08:57,328 --> 00:08:58,830
"Appointed as

114
00:09:00,498 --> 00:09:03,168
Mr. Kang's secret

115
00:09:03,877 --> 00:09:05,003
agent."

116
00:09:11,843 --> 00:09:13,552
I mean

117
00:09:13,553 --> 00:09:15,596
I stood in that pouring rain

118
00:09:15,597 --> 00:09:18,641
and worked so hard
on editing the video.

119
00:09:20,602 --> 00:09:21,770
What? A spy?

120
00:09:25,148 --> 00:09:26,316
Jeez.

121
00:09:26,649 --> 00:09:28,777
The more I get to know Mr. Kang,
the more I realize

122
00:09:30,153 --> 00:09:31,446
he's tough to read.

123
00:09:35,492 --> 00:09:37,577
2025 ONLINE FASHION SHOW FINAL REPORT

124
00:09:38,119 --> 00:09:40,038
I'm just joking.

125
00:09:40,538 --> 00:09:42,457
I can't believe you had
such a misunderstanding.

126
00:09:42,791 --> 00:09:46,211
It's not like I'm Black Widow.

127
00:09:48,296 --> 00:09:50,715
What was so funny about my apology?

128
00:09:52,342 --> 00:09:53,927
She always laughs when she sees me.

129
00:09:54,636 --> 00:09:56,805
It may be because
she feels comfortable around you.

130
00:09:57,388 --> 00:09:58,973
Jeez, you startled me.

131
00:09:59,641 --> 00:10:01,767
Alert me before you respond, Luni.

132
00:10:01,768 --> 00:10:02,977
Okay, I'm sorry.

133
00:10:07,774 --> 00:10:08,817
Anyway.

134
00:10:09,567 --> 00:10:11,401
- What did you say?
- It may be because

135
00:10:11,402 --> 00:10:13,570
she feels comfortable around you.

136
00:10:13,571 --> 00:10:17,075
Or she may have feelings for you.

137
00:10:18,910 --> 00:10:19,993
"Feelings for me"?

138
00:10:19,994 --> 00:10:20,995
I am

139
00:10:21,454 --> 00:10:22,914
on Team Ha-gi.

140
00:10:24,624 --> 00:10:28,336
I am on Team Ha-gi.

141
00:10:34,968 --> 00:10:36,093
And?

142
00:10:36,094 --> 00:10:39,430
Do you find yourself thinking
about the moments you spent together?

143
00:10:42,142 --> 00:10:43,976
- Yes.
- That means your brain

144
00:10:43,977 --> 00:10:47,688
releases a lot of dopamine
when you think of that person.

145
00:10:47,689 --> 00:10:51,233
You're in the process of forming
the early stages of attachment.

146
00:10:51,234 --> 00:10:52,569
Congratulations!

147
00:10:53,153 --> 00:10:54,236
What?

148
00:10:54,237 --> 00:10:56,864
No, it's not me. It was her.

149
00:10:56,865 --> 00:10:58,615
She was the one who laughed at me.

150
00:10:58,616 --> 00:11:00,492
That's even stronger proof.

151
00:11:00,493 --> 00:11:04,872
A woman's smile is a social cue
and a positive biological reaction.

152
00:11:04,873 --> 00:11:08,250
It must mean
your genes are quite attractive.

153
00:11:08,251 --> 00:11:09,460
Forget it. That's enough.

154
00:11:10,211 --> 00:11:11,212
OUCH!

155
00:11:12,505 --> 00:11:14,424
You're really nosy for an AI bot.

156
00:11:39,282 --> 00:11:40,824
I SCRAPED MY KNEES TODAY
WHILE POWERWALKING IN SADNESS

157
00:11:40,825 --> 00:11:42,368
THEN A GIRL CAME AND ASKED,
"ARE YOU ALL RIGHT?"

158
00:11:43,119 --> 00:11:45,704
EVERYTHING WILL GO WELL
DON'T WORRY ABOUT ANYTHING

159
00:11:45,705 --> 00:11:49,375
I'M ROOTING FOR YOU
EVERY STEP OF THE WAY

160
00:11:55,506 --> 00:11:57,717
COCOTALK
YOU HAVE A NEW MESSAGE

161
00:12:21,741 --> 00:12:22,742
What?

162
00:12:24,827 --> 00:12:25,912
What do I do?

163
00:12:28,373 --> 00:12:29,415
Girls!

164
00:12:31,793 --> 00:12:32,961
Girls, I need help.

165
00:12:33,586 --> 00:12:35,754
What do I do?

166
00:12:35,755 --> 00:12:36,839
- Why?
- What is it?

167
00:12:38,258 --> 00:12:40,467
"It's the weekend.
What are you up to?"

168
00:12:40,468 --> 00:12:41,551
CHAN

169
00:12:41,552 --> 00:12:43,680
- "Wish"?
- I know, right?

170
00:12:44,764 --> 00:12:46,975
You two also have no idea
what this means, do you?

171
00:12:49,811 --> 00:12:51,354
Why would he suddenly ask this?

172
00:12:53,064 --> 00:12:55,191
- It's clear, right?
- So obvious.

173
00:12:56,693 --> 00:12:58,695
What is?

174
00:12:59,279 --> 00:13:01,281
Namda, make up your mind.

175
00:13:02,156 --> 00:13:04,993
Will you go as a woman or as a fan?

176
00:13:05,910 --> 00:13:08,829
Show up where as a woman or a fan?

177
00:13:08,830 --> 00:13:09,998
Oh, come on!

178
00:13:10,373 --> 00:13:13,835
You're so slow.
What do you think this means?

179
00:13:14,377 --> 00:13:15,878
It's obviously a date.

180
00:13:17,422 --> 00:13:18,506
A date?

181
00:13:20,216 --> 00:13:21,968
Like an actual date?

182
00:13:24,470 --> 00:13:27,889
What do you mean
he's asking me out on a date?

183
00:13:27,890 --> 00:13:30,643
Jeez. You're so slow. Come on.

184
00:13:31,185 --> 00:13:34,689
Of course, I'll show up as a fan.
How am I a woman to him?

185
00:13:35,273 --> 00:13:36,816
Namda, listen up.

186
00:13:37,984 --> 00:13:40,445
A fan is a woman too.

187
00:13:49,495 --> 00:13:51,247
Is there a particular wine
you're looking for?

188
00:13:52,582 --> 00:13:55,335
It's not for me. It's a gift.

189
00:13:55,585 --> 00:13:57,919
But there are
way too many different kinds of wine.

190
00:13:57,920 --> 00:14:00,590
Do you know
what the other person prefers?

191
00:14:00,798 --> 00:14:03,300
No, let's see.

192
00:14:03,301 --> 00:14:05,094
He's a man in his 30s.

193
00:14:05,470 --> 00:14:08,556
And he's rather thoughtful.

194
00:14:08,973 --> 00:14:11,893
A man in his 30s
who's the thoughtful type.

195
00:14:12,435 --> 00:14:14,896
Just give me something really good.

196
00:14:15,188 --> 00:14:18,066
By the way, is this a gift
for someone you like?

197
00:14:19,317 --> 00:14:20,360
Yes.

198
00:14:26,032 --> 00:14:27,992
Sir, would you like a recommendation?

199
00:14:28,368 --> 00:14:29,869
- Shush.
- Sorry?

200
00:14:30,536 --> 00:14:32,329
- You should tell him.
- Be quiet.

201
00:14:32,330 --> 00:14:36,084
Wait, if it's for someone you like,
what wine should you get?

202
00:14:36,334 --> 00:14:39,337
I have a recommendation.
This will be perfect.

203
00:14:46,135 --> 00:14:48,596
This wine is said to help
one's love come true.

204
00:14:49,889 --> 00:14:51,599
Help love come true?

205
00:14:54,435 --> 00:14:57,979
- Gosh, it's not like that.
- It must be like that.

206
00:14:57,980 --> 00:15:00,148
- No way.
- This is it.

207
00:15:00,149 --> 00:15:02,317
- Gosh, it's not.
- But it is!

208
00:15:02,318 --> 00:15:04,236
You're holding this so tightly.

209
00:15:04,237 --> 00:15:05,696
Well, you gave it to me.

210
00:15:06,072 --> 00:15:07,990
It helps one's love come true.

211
00:15:08,449 --> 00:15:09,450
My gosh!

212
00:15:11,077 --> 00:15:13,328
CAFE RIMONDE

213
00:15:13,329 --> 00:15:15,331
It should be around here.

214
00:15:19,043 --> 00:15:20,294
FILMING IN PROGRESS
BITTER SWEET

215
00:15:21,629 --> 00:15:24,172
Bitter Sweet?
Wait, is he filming here?

216
00:15:24,173 --> 00:15:27,343
I went through so much
just to see Lee Chan.

217
00:15:27,635 --> 00:15:28,678
Whatever. I'm done.

218
00:15:29,846 --> 00:15:30,930
"Lee Chan"?

219
00:15:35,268 --> 00:15:37,145
Is he here?

220
00:15:39,397 --> 00:15:41,065
Why are you out here?

221
00:15:41,274 --> 00:15:43,817
- What?
- Come. We're about to roll.

222
00:15:43,818 --> 00:15:45,236
Why would I go?

223
00:15:45,695 --> 00:15:46,863
Aren't you an extra?

224
00:15:47,572 --> 00:15:48,739
No, I'm not.

225
00:15:49,407 --> 00:15:51,950
- No, this is the outfit.
- It's not me.

226
00:15:51,951 --> 00:15:55,163
Man, this is driving me crazy.
We need to match continuity.

227
00:15:56,497 --> 00:15:59,584
Then can you help me out just once?

228
00:16:00,084 --> 00:16:01,252
- Sorry?
- Just once.

229
00:16:01,961 --> 00:16:02,962
Me?

230
00:16:04,464 --> 00:16:05,840
- I'll take that.
- Okay.

231
00:16:06,424 --> 00:16:08,551
Now, stand here.

232
00:16:12,346 --> 00:16:13,431
Please help us out.

233
00:16:16,434 --> 00:16:19,478
Keep walking away from the camera

234
00:16:19,479 --> 00:16:21,146
and Chan will come and say

235
00:16:21,147 --> 00:16:24,484
"I'm sorry. You are not the person
I was looking for."

236
00:16:25,026 --> 00:16:26,736
We're already running out of time.

237
00:16:27,195 --> 00:16:28,696
Let's get it in one take.

238
00:16:29,030 --> 00:16:30,031
Let's roll.

239
00:16:32,241 --> 00:16:33,451
Stand by.

240
00:16:34,035 --> 00:16:35,745
And cue.

241
00:16:44,754 --> 00:16:45,921
Back to your place.

242
00:16:45,922 --> 00:16:48,715
Hey, can you walk more naturally?

243
00:16:48,716 --> 00:16:50,676
- What?
- Why is your walk so stiff?

244
00:16:51,511 --> 00:16:52,512
Okay?

245
00:16:52,803 --> 00:16:53,804
Fine.

246
00:16:54,263 --> 00:16:55,890
You must be nervous, Da-reum.

247
00:16:57,808 --> 00:17:00,436
Just relax and think
that you're walking toward me. Okay?

248
00:17:01,646 --> 00:17:02,647
You got this.

249
00:17:03,564 --> 00:17:04,856
- Okay.
- Take two.

250
00:17:04,857 --> 00:17:06,901
- Let's roll again.
- Let's roll again.

251
00:17:08,319 --> 00:17:09,445
Now, slate it.

252
00:17:10,029 --> 00:17:11,531
- And...
- Wait.

253
00:17:25,753 --> 00:17:28,256
I'm sorry. You are...

254
00:17:32,677 --> 00:17:33,886
the one I was looking for.

255
00:17:52,321 --> 00:17:55,448
What's wrong, Chan?
You got the line wrong.

256
00:17:55,449 --> 00:17:58,494
Goodness. I'm sorry.
Let me do that again. I'm sorry.

257
00:18:00,371 --> 00:18:01,664
Let's do another take.

258
00:18:14,760 --> 00:18:16,929
- Oh, wow.
- Right here.

259
00:18:19,974 --> 00:18:22,143
Seo-jun, are you putting
stickers on his face?

260
00:18:23,477 --> 00:18:25,313
Great job.
Keep doing that for me. Thanks.

261
00:18:26,939 --> 00:18:28,566
Put some more on him.

262
00:18:31,736 --> 00:18:33,945
This is great. I'm so happy.

263
00:18:33,946 --> 00:18:36,239
I'm even happier to see Ha-gi
for the first time in ages.

264
00:18:36,240 --> 00:18:37,907
I'm sorry to bother you
on your day off.

265
00:18:37,908 --> 00:18:40,577
But my kids were begging to see you

266
00:18:40,578 --> 00:18:42,288
and asked me to drag you here.

267
00:18:43,205 --> 00:18:45,957
Seo-jun and Seo-yeon,
stop bothering him now.

268
00:18:45,958 --> 00:18:47,710
You'll make
my life at work difficult.

269
00:18:48,127 --> 00:18:50,546
- Go over there and play.
- Yes, go there and run around.

270
00:18:50,963 --> 00:18:52,131
Yes, you can run all you want.

271
00:18:54,675 --> 00:18:56,093
It's okay, Seong-wook.

272
00:18:57,178 --> 00:18:59,680
It's nice to get out for a change.

273
00:19:00,306 --> 00:19:03,099
And it's nice to see
Mrs. Chae after so long.

274
00:19:03,100 --> 00:19:04,934
Gosh, that brings me back
to the old days.

275
00:19:04,935 --> 00:19:06,436
When you just started working

276
00:19:06,437 --> 00:19:10,274
you'd chase me around like a chick,
calling me, "Ms. Chae."

277
00:19:10,566 --> 00:19:13,526
And you went around
calling me, "Mr. CEO."

278
00:19:13,527 --> 00:19:15,612
If only my business hadn't failed.

279
00:19:15,613 --> 00:19:18,615
Respect him at work
and watch what you say.

280
00:19:18,616 --> 00:19:21,619
We have a mountain of debt
because of that ruined business.

281
00:19:22,078 --> 00:19:25,664
Please show my husband your favor,
CEO Kang Ha-gi.

282
00:19:25,665 --> 00:19:27,249
- A raise, please.
- Don't mention it.

283
00:19:27,833 --> 00:19:29,919
I'm so grateful for his help.

284
00:19:30,795 --> 00:19:33,130
I should've planned
this get-together sooner.

285
00:19:33,673 --> 00:19:35,465
Come over to my place.

286
00:19:35,466 --> 00:19:36,842
I'll treat you to dinner.

287
00:19:37,593 --> 00:19:41,054
Really?
I'd love to eat at your place.

288
00:19:41,055 --> 00:19:42,598
Stop. What do you mean?

289
00:19:42,848 --> 00:19:44,557
Why? What did I say just now?

290
00:19:44,558 --> 00:19:45,975
- You'd love to eat there?
- No.

291
00:19:45,976 --> 00:19:47,770
I think the kids are fighting.

292
00:19:52,108 --> 00:19:53,150
Is this it?

293
00:20:01,033 --> 00:20:02,243
I can't see anything.

294
00:20:12,670 --> 00:20:14,004
- You found it all right.
- Yes.

295
00:20:14,588 --> 00:20:15,798
- Get in.
- Okay.

296
00:20:24,473 --> 00:20:26,474
- Shall we?
- Okay.

297
00:20:26,475 --> 00:20:29,770
Just drop me at any subway station
on your way.

298
00:20:30,312 --> 00:20:31,355
What do you mean?

299
00:20:32,148 --> 00:20:33,691
- You have to grant me a wish.
- What?

300
00:20:34,483 --> 00:20:35,484
But back there...

301
00:20:37,319 --> 00:20:38,362
Did you think

302
00:20:38,946 --> 00:20:41,323
my wish was
for you to show up at my shoot?

303
00:20:45,035 --> 00:20:47,872
I wanted to get some good food
with you after the shoot.

304
00:20:48,831 --> 00:20:51,124
But the shoot ran long

305
00:20:51,125 --> 00:20:53,252
and I had to cancel my reservation.

306
00:20:56,172 --> 00:20:58,090
Come to my place. I'll cook for you.

307
00:21:01,844 --> 00:21:02,845
Pardon?

308
00:21:05,264 --> 00:21:07,641
Your place?

309
00:21:08,225 --> 00:21:09,226
Yes.

310
00:21:09,602 --> 00:21:10,895
You mean

311
00:21:11,437 --> 00:21:12,855
I'm going to your place?

312
00:21:13,397 --> 00:21:14,982
Yes, it's right around the corner.

313
00:21:16,275 --> 00:21:19,069
What's going on? Am I dreaming?

314
00:21:20,196 --> 00:21:21,489
My heart is about to burst.

315
00:21:21,989 --> 00:21:23,449
- Buckle up.
- What? Okay.

316
00:21:29,914 --> 00:21:32,332
Tech neck, rounded shoulders,
and a herniated disc too.

317
00:21:32,333 --> 00:21:33,709
You're a whole mess.

318
00:21:33,834 --> 00:21:36,378
You should pick up
a workout like Pilates.

319
00:21:36,629 --> 00:21:38,963
Why would a guy do Pilates?

320
00:21:38,964 --> 00:21:41,257
Without this curve,
my neck would be stiff.

321
00:21:41,258 --> 00:21:43,594
My shoulders are obviously straight,
and so is my back.

322
00:21:45,429 --> 00:21:46,514
I'm totally fine.

323
00:21:47,765 --> 00:21:49,683
SMOOTH

324
00:21:58,359 --> 00:22:00,402
APPARATUS PILATES
POSTURE CORRECTION

325
00:22:02,279 --> 00:22:03,530
Smooth?

326
00:22:03,531 --> 00:22:04,865
HYBRID PILATES

327
00:22:06,408 --> 00:22:07,451
The doctor was right.

328
00:22:08,744 --> 00:22:11,372
My neck hurts. It does.

329
00:22:26,929 --> 00:22:28,472
This is amazing.

330
00:22:47,032 --> 00:22:49,243
- This way.
- Okay.

331
00:22:50,953 --> 00:22:53,706
Walking into his place together

332
00:22:54,123 --> 00:22:55,749
makes us feel like a couple...

333
00:22:56,333 --> 00:22:57,710
Get a grip on yourself, Da-reum.

334
00:22:58,168 --> 00:23:01,462
He only invited me home
because he can't eat outside freely.

335
00:23:01,463 --> 00:23:03,382
Cut it out with your filthy delusion.

336
00:23:09,513 --> 00:23:10,681
What should I make?

337
00:23:12,600 --> 00:23:14,184
CREAM RISOTTO

338
00:23:15,769 --> 00:23:17,687
2022 GOLDEN CREST AWARD
BEST ACTOR LEE CHAN

339
00:23:17,688 --> 00:23:18,814
Yes, I remember.

340
00:23:28,240 --> 00:23:30,659
That was the Rookie Award he won
after he had just started acting.

341
00:23:32,536 --> 00:23:34,538
I cried a river back then.

342
00:23:38,125 --> 00:23:39,542
- Da-reum.
- Yes?

343
00:23:39,543 --> 00:23:40,920
You can go upstairs and take a tour.

344
00:23:42,046 --> 00:23:43,922
May I do that?

345
00:23:43,923 --> 00:23:45,007
Of course.

346
00:23:45,257 --> 00:23:46,467
I'll call you when I'm done.

347
00:23:47,509 --> 00:23:48,552
Okay.

348
00:23:49,929 --> 00:23:51,430
- Feel free to relax.
- Okay.

349
00:23:56,477 --> 00:23:57,519
What the heck.

350
00:23:58,187 --> 00:23:59,313
CREAM GNOCCHI

351
00:24:03,859 --> 00:24:05,986
Please excuse me.

352
00:24:13,494 --> 00:24:14,495
My gosh.

353
00:24:15,412 --> 00:24:17,915
This was the shoot
he did with Photographer Yeong-su.

354
00:24:18,248 --> 00:24:19,917
This wasn't in the pictorial.

355
00:24:20,501 --> 00:24:23,837
Am I really allowed to see
these unreleased photos?

356
00:24:26,298 --> 00:24:28,801
Look at his eyes. Insane.

357
00:24:33,222 --> 00:24:36,183
So this is where
he streams live from time to time.

358
00:24:36,642 --> 00:24:38,310
It's so cool.

359
00:24:42,982 --> 00:24:44,358
He's so great.

360
00:24:54,952 --> 00:24:57,371
Does he still make music?

361
00:24:57,830 --> 00:25:00,164
Da-reum, dinner's ready.
Come on down.

362
00:25:00,165 --> 00:25:01,166
Okay.

363
00:25:08,716 --> 00:25:10,217
CREAM GNOCCHI, FISH ROE PASTA

364
00:25:17,016 --> 00:25:20,019
Did you make all these?

365
00:25:21,687 --> 00:25:22,980
You're amazing.

366
00:25:23,188 --> 00:25:25,607
- You're teasing me.
- I'm not.

367
00:25:27,026 --> 00:25:28,318
It's fine as long as it's good.

368
00:25:29,028 --> 00:25:32,072
I tried doing my best,
but I don't know how good it is.

369
00:25:34,491 --> 00:25:35,492
Thank you.

370
00:25:42,249 --> 00:25:43,667
It's really good.

371
00:25:44,960 --> 00:25:46,586
It's like a dish
made by a famous chef.

372
00:25:46,587 --> 00:25:49,006
Really? I did get some help.

373
00:25:49,798 --> 00:25:51,884
Eat up, Da-reum. Here.

374
00:25:52,468 --> 00:25:53,594
Thank you.

375
00:26:00,517 --> 00:26:03,353
I'm too nervous
to enjoy this right now.

376
00:26:04,188 --> 00:26:05,898
I hope you weren't lying
when you said it was good.

377
00:26:09,109 --> 00:26:12,071
I'm just a bit nervous.

378
00:26:13,030 --> 00:26:15,991
- If it's too much, just leave it.
- No, it's not.

379
00:26:16,408 --> 00:26:19,161
Usually, I would've finished
all of these in three minutes.

380
00:26:22,498 --> 00:26:23,540
One second.

381
00:26:35,719 --> 00:26:37,930
YOON CHO-YI

382
00:26:47,898 --> 00:26:49,316
How's work?

383
00:26:52,694 --> 00:26:54,238
It's probably not easy
to work with Ha-gi.

384
00:26:57,699 --> 00:26:58,992
It's not.

385
00:26:59,618 --> 00:27:01,203
When he comes next to me

386
00:27:01,745 --> 00:27:03,705
I get chills down my spine.

387
00:27:05,249 --> 00:27:07,376
He's someone
I can't seem to get close to.

388
00:27:07,876 --> 00:27:09,002
He's like that.

389
00:27:09,169 --> 00:27:12,213
He never lets his guard down
around people.

390
00:27:12,214 --> 00:27:14,466
Yes, exactly.

391
00:27:14,800 --> 00:27:18,637
His office is impeccably neat
right down to every single pen.

392
00:27:19,096 --> 00:27:21,014
He's probably like that at home too.

393
00:27:21,515 --> 00:27:22,558
Right?

394
00:27:31,316 --> 00:27:32,860
Hey, this is really good.

395
00:27:33,402 --> 00:27:34,528
Eat up.

396
00:27:35,529 --> 00:27:37,114
- Go.
- Let's go.

397
00:27:37,906 --> 00:27:40,283
- Guys, no running.
- Don't you love his place?

398
00:27:40,284 --> 00:27:41,701
This isn't our place!

399
00:27:41,702 --> 00:27:43,035
- I wish it were.
- Hey.

400
00:27:43,036 --> 00:27:44,830
The one thing Ha-gi can't stand

401
00:27:45,330 --> 00:27:47,166
is anything
that's hectic and disorderly.

402
00:27:47,583 --> 00:27:49,459
He rarely ever invites people over.

403
00:27:49,710 --> 00:27:51,003
Sorry, Ha-gi.

404
00:27:51,753 --> 00:27:53,672
- It's okay.
- Stop running!

405
00:27:54,923 --> 00:27:56,008
What's this?

406
00:27:57,259 --> 00:27:59,303
- But one funny thing about him.
- Hey! No!

407
00:28:02,055 --> 00:28:03,557
- Uncle Ha-gi...
- Uncle Ha-gi...

408
00:28:09,313 --> 00:28:10,355
Fine.

409
00:28:11,607 --> 00:28:13,025
Go ahead.

410
00:28:19,406 --> 00:28:21,992
He has the weakest spot
for people within his boundary.

411
00:28:24,661 --> 00:28:26,872
He was really nosy when we were kids.

412
00:28:27,331 --> 00:28:28,457
You mean, Mr. Kang?

413
00:28:29,208 --> 00:28:30,417
That's hard to imagine.

414
00:28:32,336 --> 00:28:35,255
The reason we got close
was thanks to his nosiness.

415
00:28:36,423 --> 00:28:38,592
I wasn't looking to make friends

416
00:28:38,967 --> 00:28:40,093
but Ha-gi

417
00:28:40,886 --> 00:28:42,387
kept pestering me.

418
00:28:44,264 --> 00:28:45,933
I transferred
when I was in 10th grade

419
00:28:46,642 --> 00:28:48,018
and had trouble adapting.

420
00:28:48,977 --> 00:28:49,978
I got bullied too.

421
00:28:51,939 --> 00:28:53,899
- There you are, my friend.
- What?

422
00:28:54,816 --> 00:28:55,900
What are you doing?

423
00:28:55,901 --> 00:28:57,152
Time to pay
this week's friendship fee.

424
00:28:57,402 --> 00:28:58,487
Cut it out.

425
00:29:00,697 --> 00:29:01,698
Thanks a lot.

426
00:29:05,160 --> 00:29:06,328
Oh, sorry.

427
00:29:06,536 --> 00:29:08,163
He's a player on my team.

428
00:29:08,372 --> 00:29:09,998
Do you have business with him?

429
00:29:11,291 --> 00:29:12,875
Darn it.

430
00:29:12,876 --> 00:29:15,503
Ha-gi was the school president,
who got good grades

431
00:29:15,504 --> 00:29:17,630
and was good at basketball.
The typical golden boy.

432
00:29:17,631 --> 00:29:18,632
Let's go.

433
00:29:20,384 --> 00:29:21,551
I'll get you later.

434
00:29:30,060 --> 00:29:31,061
Hey.

435
00:29:32,396 --> 00:29:34,314
We really need
more players on our team.

436
00:29:35,023 --> 00:29:36,191
Can you play one game with us?

437
00:29:37,109 --> 00:29:38,110
What?

438
00:29:39,236 --> 00:29:41,279
- Come on.
- Let's split into teams.

439
00:29:41,280 --> 00:29:42,697
- Okay.
- Come on.

440
00:29:42,698 --> 00:29:44,783
The losers treat the winners
to snacks at the snack bar.

441
00:29:45,117 --> 00:29:46,952
- Let's go.
- Come on.

442
00:29:57,337 --> 00:29:58,380
Hey, Chan.

443
00:29:58,964 --> 00:29:59,965
Time for a snack bar run.

444
00:30:04,720 --> 00:30:05,721
Hey.

445
00:30:06,513 --> 00:30:07,889
What are you waiting for? Let's go.

446
00:30:08,849 --> 00:30:09,891
What?

447
00:30:10,434 --> 00:30:13,520
- Come on.
- And he was a warm-hearted kid

448
00:30:13,770 --> 00:30:15,647
who couldn't see anyone get left out.

449
00:30:20,444 --> 00:30:21,945
- Go, Ha-gi.
- Go, Ha-gi.

450
00:30:22,237 --> 00:30:24,530
Over here!

451
00:30:24,531 --> 00:30:27,200
- Nice job!
- Oh, no.

452
00:30:28,535 --> 00:30:29,994
You got this, Ha-gi.

453
00:30:29,995 --> 00:30:31,413
Just do your thing. Yes.

454
00:30:31,663 --> 00:30:32,914
Yes, that's it.

455
00:30:33,290 --> 00:30:35,334
- Nice job!
- Okay!

456
00:30:35,959 --> 00:30:37,252
Great job!

457
00:30:39,921 --> 00:30:41,297
Nice job!

458
00:30:41,298 --> 00:30:43,257
That was awesome, Ha-gi!

459
00:30:43,258 --> 00:30:44,968
- Awesome job.
- Let's go.

460
00:30:47,429 --> 00:30:49,973
Thanks to him,
I gradually changed too.

461
00:30:51,141 --> 00:30:53,727
- Hey, wait.
- Let's go!

462
00:30:54,227 --> 00:30:55,437
What do you want to eat?

463
00:30:55,854 --> 00:30:57,146
What do you feel like?

464
00:30:57,147 --> 00:30:58,565
It was a lot of fun

465
00:30:58,774 --> 00:31:01,234
- to spend time with Ha-gi.
- I don't know. What should we eat?

466
00:31:01,985 --> 00:31:04,362
I even stuck around at his place
and had dinner every day.

467
00:31:04,363 --> 00:31:05,447
It smells great.

468
00:31:05,697 --> 00:31:08,157
- My parents always came home late.
- Thank you.

469
00:31:08,158 --> 00:31:09,493
Thank you.

470
00:31:09,868 --> 00:31:11,118
Hey, you made bulgogi.

471
00:31:11,119 --> 00:31:12,829
Yes, because it's your favorite.

472
00:31:27,844 --> 00:31:28,845
Eat up.

473
00:31:36,436 --> 00:31:37,896
Just as you helped me

474
00:31:39,189 --> 00:31:41,066
overcome my darkest times

475
00:31:42,692 --> 00:31:44,903
you had Mr. Kang with you.

476
00:31:46,655 --> 00:31:47,781
He is

477
00:31:48,573 --> 00:31:50,659
my one and only friend.

478
00:31:53,078 --> 00:31:55,538
Maybe everyone wanted
to be friends with you

479
00:31:55,539 --> 00:31:57,666
but you just didn't realize it?

480
00:31:58,250 --> 00:32:00,293
No way. I wasn't that popular.

481
00:32:01,461 --> 00:32:03,171
- You're lying.
- I'm serious.

482
00:32:03,672 --> 00:32:05,257
Ha-gi was much more popular.

483
00:32:05,799 --> 00:32:06,800
Really?

484
00:32:08,176 --> 00:32:10,011
I guess it shows

485
00:32:11,888 --> 00:32:14,015
whether a person
has always been loved

486
00:32:17,519 --> 00:32:18,728
or they haven't.

487
00:32:26,361 --> 00:32:28,196
Everyone leaves me in the end.

488
00:32:30,574 --> 00:32:31,700
I wouldn't.

489
00:32:32,701 --> 00:32:34,453
For the last ten years... No.

490
00:32:35,120 --> 00:32:36,163
To be exact

491
00:32:37,038 --> 00:32:39,540
I've liked only you
for the last 11 years and ten months.

492
00:32:39,541 --> 00:32:42,042
I have never set my eyes
on anyone else, not even once.

493
00:32:42,043 --> 00:32:44,713
And I will continue to like only you.

494
00:32:49,259 --> 00:32:52,262
Wait, what have I done just now?

495
00:32:52,971 --> 00:32:56,057
Look how overwhelmed he is.

496
00:32:57,058 --> 00:32:58,185
I mean

497
00:32:59,269 --> 00:33:00,394
as a fan.

498
00:33:00,395 --> 00:33:01,855
Completely as a fan.

499
00:33:02,355 --> 00:33:04,483
Just as a fan.

500
00:33:18,288 --> 00:33:19,414
Thanks for liking me.

501
00:33:21,291 --> 00:33:22,626
I'm not even a big deal

502
00:33:23,710 --> 00:33:26,046
but thank you for your support
over such a long time.

503
00:33:26,421 --> 00:33:27,506
Thank you.

504
00:33:27,881 --> 00:33:29,508
I want to thank you too.

505
00:33:31,551 --> 00:33:35,555
And I never thought
I'd see a day like this in my life.

506
00:33:37,641 --> 00:33:38,642
Da-reum.

507
00:33:39,059 --> 00:33:40,268
Can I ask you for a favor?

508
00:34:04,626 --> 00:34:05,835
What do you think about this song?

509
00:34:07,712 --> 00:34:09,005
I love it.

510
00:34:10,006 --> 00:34:13,510
It reminds me of old D.N.X songs.

511
00:34:16,137 --> 00:34:17,389
D.N.X.

512
00:34:18,974 --> 00:34:21,560
I only meant how the song sounded.

513
00:34:23,478 --> 00:34:24,563
I'm sorry.

514
00:34:24,729 --> 00:34:26,272
I shouldn't have brought it up.

515
00:34:26,273 --> 00:34:27,607
No, don't say that.

516
00:34:28,900 --> 00:34:30,360
I'm so grateful

517
00:34:30,735 --> 00:34:32,696
that you still think about D.N.X.

518
00:34:37,492 --> 00:34:38,535
Da-reum.

519
00:34:40,537 --> 00:34:42,497
Do you also want us to reunite?

520
00:34:43,832 --> 00:34:45,083
Yes, of course.

521
00:34:45,458 --> 00:34:47,586
All D-Angels would feel the same.

522
00:34:49,921 --> 00:34:52,507
It's actually meant
to be a D.N.X fan song.

523
00:34:54,759 --> 00:34:56,595
If we ever reunite

524
00:34:57,137 --> 00:34:58,513
I want to sing it with everyone.

525
00:35:00,640 --> 00:35:01,683
Chan...

526
00:35:02,559 --> 00:35:04,226
I also did the mixing.
Would you like to listen to it?

527
00:35:04,227 --> 00:35:06,104
Oh, yes. I'd love to listen to it.

528
00:35:23,079 --> 00:35:24,164
What's this?

529
00:35:25,040 --> 00:35:26,166
What is this vibe?

530
00:35:32,922 --> 00:35:35,425
You're so slow.
What do you think this means?

531
00:35:35,634 --> 00:35:37,636
It's obviously a date.

532
00:35:37,844 --> 00:35:39,554
A fan is a woman too.

533
00:35:40,680 --> 00:35:41,890
What do I do?

534
00:35:57,322 --> 00:35:58,323
- Da-reum.
- Yes?

535
00:36:08,166 --> 00:36:09,542
What are you guys doing?

536
00:36:15,048 --> 00:36:16,174
What are you doing here?

537
00:36:16,925 --> 00:36:18,635
Am I in the wrong place?

538
00:36:21,471 --> 00:36:22,889
Is it you this time?

539
00:36:23,431 --> 00:36:24,891
How was the fan meet with him?

540
00:36:25,558 --> 00:36:27,102
Did you enjoy it
to your heart's content?

541
00:36:27,894 --> 00:36:29,896
- Pardon?
- Come out. Let's talk outside.

542
00:36:31,022 --> 00:36:32,023
Did I

543
00:36:32,607 --> 00:36:35,109
walk in
when you were expecting something?

544
00:36:35,110 --> 00:36:36,111
Hey, Yoon Cho-yi.

545
00:36:41,408 --> 00:36:43,785
Oh, no. I guess I was right.

546
00:36:45,954 --> 00:36:48,123
Did you really think
there was something going on?

547
00:36:52,168 --> 00:36:54,921
- She's cute.
- What are you saying? Get out.

548
00:36:55,630 --> 00:36:57,507
No, I'll leave.

549
00:37:02,262 --> 00:37:03,763
Thank you for everything today,
Director Lee.

550
00:37:03,972 --> 00:37:06,182
I'm sorry, but if you don't mind,
I'll get going first.

551
00:37:07,100 --> 00:37:08,143
Da-reum.

552
00:37:13,022 --> 00:37:14,065
Da-reum.

553
00:37:24,033 --> 00:37:25,034
Da-reum.

554
00:37:35,462 --> 00:37:37,505
Chan, I'm sorry.

555
00:37:37,881 --> 00:37:39,507
I was such a bother today.

556
00:37:40,133 --> 00:37:41,508
You should get inside.

557
00:37:41,509 --> 00:37:44,137
- Da-reum, that's not it...
- Chan.

558
00:37:44,721 --> 00:37:45,764
Can you

559
00:37:46,973 --> 00:37:49,100
just let me go?

560
00:37:50,393 --> 00:37:51,436
I feel

561
00:37:53,938 --> 00:37:55,732
mortified right now.

562
00:38:36,689 --> 00:38:38,817
Why did I dress up?

563
00:38:40,985 --> 00:38:42,237
This is humiliating.

564
00:39:09,305 --> 00:39:10,598
How did you get in?

565
00:39:12,976 --> 00:39:15,186
The passcode to your door is
still the same.

566
00:39:16,855 --> 00:39:18,773
You must've kept it
because you wanted me to come in.

567
00:39:21,776 --> 00:39:23,111
The person who was just here...

568
00:39:24,153 --> 00:39:26,739
I had her over for a meal
because she was a special fan.

569
00:39:28,241 --> 00:39:30,285
She's not someone
you can talk to like that.

570
00:39:30,535 --> 00:39:33,371
Have you ever had me over
for anything when we were dating?

571
00:39:33,913 --> 00:39:35,163
What does she mean to you?

572
00:39:35,164 --> 00:39:36,915
Why are you treating her
like she's special?

573
00:39:36,916 --> 00:39:40,211
She rooted for me for ten years,
but I've never done anything for her.

574
00:39:41,671 --> 00:39:42,672
Right.

575
00:39:42,922 --> 00:39:44,632
You have always been like that.

576
00:39:44,883 --> 00:39:47,427
You act like a good person
on the outside.

577
00:39:48,094 --> 00:39:50,638
You think you won't hurt other people
like you hurt me?

578
00:39:51,264 --> 00:39:53,016
Whoever you choose to date

579
00:39:53,683 --> 00:39:54,726
you'll still be the same.

580
00:39:59,606 --> 00:40:02,357
Ha-gi, thanks for everything today.
See you next time.

581
00:40:02,358 --> 00:40:03,734
- Bye.
- Say bye to Uncle Ha-gi.

582
00:40:03,735 --> 00:40:05,110
- Bye.
- Bye, Uncle Ha-gi.

583
00:40:05,111 --> 00:40:06,653
See you.

584
00:40:06,654 --> 00:40:08,697
- Bye.
- Take care.

585
00:40:08,698 --> 00:40:11,826
See you. Bye.

586
00:40:20,710 --> 00:40:22,420
A sticker remover.

587
00:40:24,297 --> 00:40:25,298
Where can I get it?

588
00:40:36,601 --> 00:40:38,728
BEAUTY TRIO GROUP CHAT

589
00:40:39,312 --> 00:40:42,272
Namda! Are you still with Chan?

590
00:40:42,273 --> 00:40:44,776
Are you alive or not?
Why aren't you answering?

591
00:40:53,910 --> 00:40:56,496
BITTER SWEET

592
00:40:58,414 --> 00:41:02,293
I hope they aren't fighting
because of me.

593
00:41:04,545 --> 00:41:05,672
I doubt it.

594
00:41:06,381 --> 00:41:07,548
I mean nothing to them.

595
00:41:09,801 --> 00:41:14,889
BITTER SWEET

596
00:41:17,767 --> 00:41:20,061
Oh, no. I guess I was right.

597
00:41:20,895 --> 00:41:23,022
Did you really think
there was something going on?

598
00:41:27,902 --> 00:41:29,195
This is humiliating.

599
00:41:30,488 --> 00:41:32,532
Come to your senses, Nam Da-reum.

600
00:41:33,408 --> 00:41:35,660
You're just one of his numerous fans.

601
00:42:04,439 --> 00:42:08,651
INCOMING CALL
CHAN

602
00:42:25,209 --> 00:42:26,794
Where on earth can I get it?

603
00:42:50,777 --> 00:42:51,778
Wait...

604
00:43:11,214 --> 00:43:12,215
Ms. Nam!

605
00:43:33,194 --> 00:43:34,195
Are you okay?

606
00:43:35,863 --> 00:43:36,864
Yes.

607
00:43:44,080 --> 00:43:45,456
Why aren't you watching
where you're going?

608
00:43:45,832 --> 00:43:47,875
Why did you cross the road
without checking the traffic light?

609
00:43:53,297 --> 00:43:54,382
I'm sorry.

610
00:43:57,426 --> 00:43:59,637
I couldn't see it.

611
00:44:02,348 --> 00:44:03,391
I really

612
00:44:04,600 --> 00:44:06,227
didn't see it.

613
00:44:11,232 --> 00:44:13,025
I know I was wrong.

614
00:44:14,902 --> 00:44:17,738
If you yell at me like that

615
00:44:21,576 --> 00:44:23,744
I don't know what to say.

616
00:44:40,553 --> 00:44:41,679
Sorry for getting mad at you.

617
00:44:43,014 --> 00:44:44,015
I was startled too.

618
00:44:46,517 --> 00:44:49,061
No, I'm sorry.

619
00:44:50,188 --> 00:44:51,230
Did

620
00:44:52,273 --> 00:44:53,274
something bad happen?

621
00:44:56,777 --> 00:44:57,820
No.

622
00:44:58,446 --> 00:45:01,157
Today was
the happiest day of my life.

623
00:45:06,829 --> 00:45:07,872
Something

624
00:45:09,207 --> 00:45:11,125
I'd always dreamed of
happened to me.

625
00:45:13,419 --> 00:45:14,462
But

626
00:45:15,880 --> 00:45:19,175
I didn't realize dreams end...

627
00:45:22,470 --> 00:45:23,471
once I wake up.

628
00:45:37,610 --> 00:45:38,611
Let's go.

629
00:45:39,153 --> 00:45:40,196
I'll take you home.

630
00:45:41,030 --> 00:45:42,031
Okay.

631
00:45:45,618 --> 00:45:46,619
Your bag.

632
00:45:47,119 --> 00:45:48,120
Oh, that's right.

633
00:45:53,668 --> 00:45:54,794
What's wrong with me?

634
00:46:05,179 --> 00:46:06,263
INKUK HOSPITAL

635
00:46:06,264 --> 00:46:07,306
You sprained your ligament.

636
00:46:07,974 --> 00:46:09,767
You need to wear it
for at least two weeks.

637
00:46:29,662 --> 00:46:31,956
I'm sorry. It's my fault.

638
00:46:36,794 --> 00:46:39,964
These are what I could find for now.
I thought you might need them.

639
00:46:42,091 --> 00:46:43,134
What are they?

640
00:46:56,355 --> 00:46:58,024
RUBBER GLOVES

641
00:47:02,987 --> 00:47:04,071
What's this for?

642
00:47:16,792 --> 00:47:20,170
Shower with that on for tonight.
And tomorrow...

643
00:47:20,171 --> 00:47:21,255
Take this off now.

644
00:47:22,673 --> 00:47:23,716
Okay.

645
00:47:24,717 --> 00:47:26,052
I'll take it off.

646
00:47:46,364 --> 00:47:47,531
Oh, Mr. Kang.

647
00:47:49,283 --> 00:47:51,410
Mr. Kang, let me help you.

648
00:47:53,162 --> 00:47:54,163
Are you okay?

649
00:47:56,207 --> 00:47:59,250
Whenever I'm with you,
I have to watch my back and front.

650
00:47:59,251 --> 00:48:00,628
I just can't let my guard down.

651
00:48:02,213 --> 00:48:03,506
I'd better get going.

652
00:48:04,382 --> 00:48:06,759
I'm sorry, Mr. Kang.

653
00:48:08,719 --> 00:48:11,972
What am I going to do now?
I got into trouble again.

654
00:48:28,614 --> 00:48:29,657
Well...

655
00:48:30,074 --> 00:48:33,494
He just wanted to thank me
for being his fan for so long.

656
00:48:33,828 --> 00:48:37,330
We had dinner at his house.
That's all.

657
00:48:37,331 --> 00:48:39,083
Wait, you went to his house?

658
00:48:39,708 --> 00:48:41,585
How can you say
that's not a big deal?

659
00:48:41,794 --> 00:48:45,798
Normally, you would've made a scene
saying you couldn't believe it.

660
00:48:46,298 --> 00:48:47,425
But why are you so calm?

661
00:48:48,968 --> 00:48:51,011
- You're suspicious.
- You're suspicious.

662
00:48:54,223 --> 00:48:56,183
No, I'm not.

663
00:48:57,143 --> 00:48:59,812
I couldn't be happier.
I'm on cloud nine.

664
00:49:01,939 --> 00:49:06,026
When you experience
something completely unbelievable

665
00:49:06,527 --> 00:49:09,113
you become surprisingly calm.

666
00:49:13,075 --> 00:49:15,453
If that's the case,
I'm happy for you.

667
00:49:15,995 --> 00:49:17,329
I was worried for nothing.

668
00:49:23,002 --> 00:49:25,588
Did you see Namda's terrible acting?

669
00:49:28,299 --> 00:49:29,425
Something happened for sure.

670
00:49:30,092 --> 00:49:31,217
Something happened to her.

671
00:49:31,218 --> 00:49:33,137
She was excited to meet Chan.

672
00:49:34,138 --> 00:49:35,848
What the heck happened?

673
00:49:56,785 --> 00:49:58,787
I wonder if Mr. Kang is okay.

674
00:50:03,918 --> 00:50:07,004
He'd think I'm a total nuisance.

675
00:50:09,757 --> 00:50:13,218
He wouldn't use those red gloves.
What was I thinking?

676
00:50:13,219 --> 00:50:14,595
I'm such an idiot.

677
00:50:40,454 --> 00:50:43,248
So what happened to your arm?

678
00:50:43,249 --> 00:50:44,749
It was fine until the weekend.

679
00:50:44,750 --> 00:50:46,168
A dog came at me.

680
00:50:46,585 --> 00:50:49,463
How big was the dog
to leave your arm like that?

681
00:50:56,804 --> 00:50:57,805
Well, it was

682
00:50:59,348 --> 00:51:00,765
about the size of a Pomeranian.

683
00:51:00,766 --> 00:51:02,977
A Pomeranian?

684
00:51:03,852 --> 00:51:05,520
You mean a Pomeranian?

685
00:51:05,521 --> 00:51:06,522
Mr. Kang.

686
00:51:06,855 --> 00:51:08,107
We have a seat for you here.

687
00:51:09,316 --> 00:51:10,985
Come on. Join us.

688
00:51:15,155 --> 00:51:16,240
Have a seat.

689
00:51:19,827 --> 00:51:23,288
Excuse me. We'll get beef brisket
doenjang soup and jeyuk.

690
00:51:23,289 --> 00:51:24,331
Okay.

691
00:51:25,874 --> 00:51:27,209
Mr. Kang, your arm...

692
00:51:28,460 --> 00:51:30,712
Mr. Kang, what happened to your arm?

693
00:51:30,713 --> 00:51:32,005
Let me tell you what happened.

694
00:51:32,006 --> 00:51:34,424
A Pomeranian attacked his arm.

695
00:51:34,425 --> 00:51:36,801
- A Pomeranian?
- Yes, a Pomeranian.

696
00:51:36,802 --> 00:51:39,221
- The small dog?
- Yes, the small dog.

697
00:51:40,139 --> 00:51:42,223
- The cute one?
- Very cute.

698
00:51:42,224 --> 00:51:44,392
A lovely Pomeranian?

699
00:51:44,393 --> 00:51:46,186
The lovely Pomeranian.

700
00:51:51,108 --> 00:51:53,193
I fell.

701
00:51:54,069 --> 00:51:57,948
It must be uncomfortable, Mr. Kang.

702
00:51:58,991 --> 00:52:01,534
Still, you're lucky
it's your left arm

703
00:52:01,535 --> 00:52:02,911
not your right arm.

704
00:52:03,495 --> 00:52:04,663
I'm left-handed.

705
00:52:05,164 --> 00:52:07,583
Oh, I see.

706
00:52:08,626 --> 00:52:10,835
Let's eat.

707
00:52:10,836 --> 00:52:12,546
- Enjoy.
- Enjoy your meal.

708
00:52:17,801 --> 00:52:20,512
Oh, no. What do we do?

709
00:52:21,263 --> 00:52:22,805
- Here.
- Thank you.

710
00:52:22,806 --> 00:52:24,183
I'm worried.

711
00:52:28,812 --> 00:52:30,689
Mr. Kang.

712
00:52:30,856 --> 00:52:32,441
Do you want me to feed you?

713
00:52:34,818 --> 00:52:36,235
No, thank you.

714
00:52:36,236 --> 00:52:38,572
You're eating nothing but rice.

715
00:52:38,864 --> 00:52:39,947
I like rice.

716
00:52:39,948 --> 00:52:42,159
No, let me feed you. Here.

717
00:53:13,565 --> 00:53:19,195
Mr. Kang, the overseas VC wants
to hear back from us by today.

718
00:53:19,196 --> 00:53:20,697
If you confirm it

719
00:53:20,698 --> 00:53:22,824
I'll send the file now.
What do you think?

720
00:53:22,825 --> 00:53:24,243
I want to fix a few pages.

721
00:53:24,910 --> 00:53:25,994
Give me a few minutes.

722
00:53:26,537 --> 00:53:27,538
Bye.

723
00:53:46,557 --> 00:53:47,558
Shoot.

724
00:53:56,358 --> 00:53:57,401
APPELLO CEO KANG HA-GI

725
00:53:58,068 --> 00:54:02,656
Mr. Kang, I'm sorry about all the...

726
00:54:04,158 --> 00:54:05,451
No.

727
00:54:06,869 --> 00:54:07,953
What should I say?

728
00:54:11,457 --> 00:54:15,335
Mr. Kang, if you need anything,
call me anytime...

729
00:54:16,545 --> 00:54:18,130
No.

730
00:54:19,590 --> 00:54:22,008
Why do I keep causing Mr. Kang harm

731
00:54:22,009 --> 00:54:24,845
and nothing ever works out
when I'm with him?

732
00:54:26,513 --> 00:54:27,931
What should I say in the apology?

733
00:54:30,934 --> 00:54:34,146
Think. Think with your brain.

734
00:54:36,982 --> 00:54:37,983
CALLING APPELLO CEO KANG HA-GI

735
00:54:39,818 --> 00:54:40,819
INCOMING CALL
MS. NAM DA-REUM

736
00:54:49,870 --> 00:54:50,871
Hello?

737
00:54:52,748 --> 00:54:53,749
Hello?

738
00:54:54,458 --> 00:54:55,459
Ms. Nam?

739
00:54:56,794 --> 00:54:57,878
Ms. Nam Da-reum?

740
00:54:59,755 --> 00:55:02,048
Yes, Mr. Kang.

741
00:55:02,049 --> 00:55:03,383
You must be off work by now.

742
00:55:03,509 --> 00:55:05,803
Yes. What are you calling me for
at this hour?

743
00:55:07,137 --> 00:55:08,680
Well, that's...

744
00:55:11,600 --> 00:55:13,519
Your arm must be causing you
a lot of discomfort.

745
00:55:13,852 --> 00:55:16,354
I meant to text you
because I was concerned.

746
00:55:16,355 --> 00:55:18,524
But somehow I ended up calling you.

747
00:55:19,691 --> 00:55:22,027
Yes, it's very uncomfortable.

748
00:55:24,238 --> 00:55:25,447
Because of my arm

749
00:55:26,490 --> 00:55:28,283
I couldn't even fix
the urgent proposal.

750
00:55:29,993 --> 00:55:31,078
Really?

751
00:55:33,497 --> 00:55:35,456
That's not good.

752
00:55:35,457 --> 00:55:37,333
I'll go to your house now.

753
00:55:37,334 --> 00:55:39,461
- We live in the same neighborhood.
- What?

754
00:55:40,712 --> 00:55:41,755
But...

755
00:55:42,756 --> 00:55:44,757
You could just help me
at a cafe nearby...

756
00:55:44,758 --> 00:55:46,634
No, you have an injured arm.

757
00:55:46,635 --> 00:55:49,054
How would you bring your laptop
and materials with you?

758
00:55:50,138 --> 00:55:52,306
Just wait. I'll leave soon.

759
00:55:52,307 --> 00:55:53,433
Ms. Nam Da-reum. Nam...

760
00:55:53,725 --> 00:55:55,269
Ms. Nam... Ms. Nam?

761
00:56:06,530 --> 00:56:07,656
Shoot.

762
00:56:26,258 --> 00:56:29,303
This is my chance to make up
for being a nuisance.

763
00:56:29,720 --> 00:56:31,888
Mr. Kang, just wait.

764
00:56:31,889 --> 00:56:34,182
My 600-character-per-minute fingers
are coming.

765
00:56:38,562 --> 00:56:41,106
This is Ha-gi's favorite wine.

766
00:56:51,283 --> 00:56:52,534
I'm here.

767
00:56:57,039 --> 00:56:59,458
Mr. Kang, I'm here.

768
00:57:00,834 --> 00:57:01,835
Okay.

769
00:57:09,760 --> 00:57:12,763
- Hello.
- Ms. Nam.

770
00:57:13,180 --> 00:57:14,890
- That was fast.
- Yes.

771
00:57:15,390 --> 00:57:17,558
Your house is so close.

772
00:57:17,559 --> 00:57:19,478
It's only 500m away from my house.

773
00:57:21,063 --> 00:57:22,814
- Did you run here?
- Yes.

774
00:57:23,065 --> 00:57:24,441
You need to send the proposal soon.

775
00:57:40,290 --> 00:57:41,917
Oh, thank you.

776
00:57:46,672 --> 00:57:48,465
- Where do you want me to work on it?
- What?

777
00:57:50,425 --> 00:57:53,094
Here. No, there.

778
00:57:53,095 --> 00:57:55,389
Oh, how about next to your laptop?

779
00:58:20,998 --> 00:58:23,750
- Mr. Kang, are you okay?
- Yes, I'm okay.

780
00:58:28,213 --> 00:58:29,673
- Mr. Kang.
- Yes?

781
00:58:30,298 --> 00:58:31,341
Is this the one?

782
00:58:32,843 --> 00:58:34,428
Oh, yes.

783
00:58:34,761 --> 00:58:35,762
Then...

784
00:58:38,015 --> 00:58:40,225
It's inconvenient
to look at the monitors this way.

785
00:58:41,351 --> 00:58:42,644
I'll move next to you.

786
00:58:55,157 --> 00:58:56,700
What do you need to add?

787
00:59:00,746 --> 00:59:02,247
- Mr. Kang?
- Yes?

788
00:59:03,206 --> 00:59:04,374
Did you hear what I said?

789
00:59:05,250 --> 00:59:06,460
You need to tell me what to add.

790
00:59:07,919 --> 00:59:09,212
Oh, yes. Right.

791
00:59:10,964 --> 00:59:13,341
- How did I miss that?
- Focus.

792
00:59:14,468 --> 00:59:15,469
Okay.

793
00:59:16,386 --> 00:59:17,387
Focus.

794
00:59:18,597 --> 00:59:21,140
I wanted to add some data
to the original pitch deck.

795
00:59:21,141 --> 00:59:24,269
The CEO of this VC considers
CSR important.

796
00:59:25,645 --> 00:59:28,355
Are you trying to emphasize

797
00:59:28,356 --> 00:59:29,816
Appello's mission of mutual growth?

798
00:59:30,692 --> 00:59:32,444
Yes, that's correct.

799
00:59:32,652 --> 00:59:36,239
Then, how about using the last
online fashion show as an example?

800
00:59:38,575 --> 00:59:40,868
